#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133896 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133712 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8644454b-ee25-59fd-ae65-9770a0b44442" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing the Area Bounded by a Closed Curve Using Green’s Theorem"}] :question/id #uuid "74c9ecfb-5005-53ff-b7a9-db798488587b" :question/math-academy-id "e-9554" :question/problem "Let $D$ be the region enclosed by the curve $C$ parametrized as\n$\\mathbf{r}(t) = \\langle 2\\sin t, \\: 2 \\cos t \\rangle$ for $t \\in \\left [0, 2\\pi \\right).$ \nThe area of $D$ can be written as\n\n![](images/45/45513e4aedd37b868d2020cbbb47f49938f6ca03487ded8b5e519a2ec8e4edf5.svg)\n\nwhere $P(x,y) = -y$ and $Q(x,y) = 0.$ Determine the missing part of the equation.\n\n*Hint: Note that $C$ is negatively oriented.*\n\n![](images/a5/a5eeb5db90f9ee0d86a49e5bbf02629c7886fa019db7cff3c4d0e1eb43e8fd75.png)" :question/worked-solution "Our simple, smooth, closed path $C$ is negatively oriented, and  \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x} - \\dfrac{\\partial P}{\\partial y} = 0 - \\left(-1\\right) = 1.\n$$\n\nSo, according to Green's theorem, we can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nNotice that we have to take the line integral with a minus sign since the path is negatively oriented.\n\nSubstituting $P(x,y) = -y$ and $Q(x,y) = 0,$ we get\n\n$$\n- \\oint\\limits_C P \\: \\text{d}x + Q \\: \\text{d}y = \\oint\\limits_C y \\: \\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe derivative of $\\mathbf r(t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}'(t) = \\left\\langle  2\\cos t ,\\:  -2 \\sin t \\right\\rangle.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }4{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $4\\cos^2 t.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8644454b-ee25-59fd-ae65-9770a0b44442" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050666}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523014 :question-generator/id #uuid "c4e18406-dc62-5d93-a5b4-7de04271fe9b" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186133896.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134377 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8644454b-ee25-59fd-ae65-9770a0b44442" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing the Area Bounded by a Closed Curve Using Green’s Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1997d82a-e8fd-5876-bff6-f2a494d2c16e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510841} {:answer/id #uuid "2e996338-8bd4-5f85-acba-798d27184bb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510881} {:answer/id #uuid "91c650e3-c5a3-551b-acac-5cc206d90d87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511082} {:answer/id #uuid "a50bd914-811d-5009-9a3f-16c3d9e26a55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511129} {:answer/id #uuid "e5105f35-40d7-5290-bc6b-8489218cf6ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511263}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5105f35-40d7-5290-bc6b-8489218cf6ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511263} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f782c02-0bd7-576d-a703-443eb8f872fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132301}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "097af826-94c0-5b59-ad65-7d59555aa9e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-42221" :question/problem "![](images/44/4408d1fcee1d168c6ab21ea53cf24845093bad9cc608299a36f0510c1636cc03.png)\n\nLet $D$ be the region enclosed by the curve $C$ parametrized as\n$r(t)=⟨{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t},\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}⟩$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ].$ The area of $D$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})dA={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\boxed{}\\,dt,\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x,y)=0$ and $Q(x,y)=x.$ Determine the missing part of the equation." :question/worked-solution "Our simple, smooth, closed path $C$ is positively oriented, and  \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1-0=1.\n$$\n\nSo, according to Green's theorem, we can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nSubstituting $P(x,y)=0$ and $Q(x,y)=x,$ we get\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y={∮}_{C}x\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is\n\n$$\n{r}^{′}(t)=⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134378 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8644454b-ee25-59fd-ae65-9770a0b44442" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing the Area Bounded by a Closed Curve Using Green’s Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b99d9fa-8746-5b24-b150-3778d2789fbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6\\cos^{2} t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132308} {:answer/id #uuid "4f557510-890d-5c72-baca-50a8aed5cc6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6\\sin^{2} t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132309} {:answer/id #uuid "656aa773-8708-58ce-aa12-99b62f7bf252" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\cos^{2} t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132310} {:answer/id #uuid "66e986c0-94a1-5f87-83fb-83d5fe3f5305" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6\\sin t\\cos t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132311} {:answer/id #uuid "6dca153e-7fc2-5baf-9c77-fca9326e5002" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sin t\\cos t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132312}] :answer-field/id #uuid "ff01fd58-b994-5d7c-8628-db2542bb8485" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132307} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9daf741d-ed1d-5418-9a08-c962cd04f234" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6{sin}^{2}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392496} {:answer/id #uuid "29dfbde4-ae70-5670-a1c3-f06b16942b59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392497} {:answer/id #uuid "3efa1f4b-972e-5984-9ba9-47ae745edcc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6{cos}^{2}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392498} {:answer/id #uuid "607a8eb7-ea64-55b5-903c-5325b01df2c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392499} {:answer/id #uuid "de2df677-