nTherefore, we can write our line integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }6{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369413 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8644454b-ee25-59fd-ae65-9770a0b44442" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing the Area Bounded by a Closed Curve Using Green’s Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "396b8bd9-301b-51ec-aca0-06cdba5ad003" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369415} {:answer/id #uuid "a8dbb119-5910-5170-9d33-e634a7d5b88b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369416} {:answer/id #uuid "d7ec21fa-558f-57a8-81bd-b660d625d1a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{e}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369417} {:answer/id #uuid "1a2f5977-a0c7-5e88-b88d-158811b0198d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369418} {:answer/id #uuid "f3580aca-f980-54b4-b266-0dffc5f943b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369419}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8dbb119-5910-5170-9d33-e634a7d5b88b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369416} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff67740a-3837-5c9c-8e44-2824507f3d72" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186